# component: resizable
# decisions: A11Y-2, DOC-1, DOC-2, FOC-1, FOC-6
# hunks:
#   FOC-1, FOC-6: `focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:outline-hidden`
#     goes from `ResizableHandle`. `outline-hidden` is the v3 spelling of 'no outline', so
#     upstream suppressed the one focus affordance this system has on a control that is
#     keyboard-operable (arrow keys resize it). `ring-offset-background` is left alone: it paints
#     nothing without a ring width and is upstream's own class.
#   A11Y-2: the handle's invisible hit area grows from `after:w-1` / `after:h-1` (4px) to
#     `after:w-6` / `after:h-6` (24px). The VISIBLE divider stays the 1px hairline upstream draws;
#     what changes is the strip a pointer can grab, which the geometry lane measured at 4.5px
#     across every resizable fixture — a drag target a fifth of the floor. 24px is the value the
#     pre-reset handle used and the one the lane's own `resizableNested` exclusion is written
#     against.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file, and `registry-stamp.mjs` writes the provenance header the
#               three-copy model needs (DOC-1); those hunks carry no decision of their own.
